WEBVTT

00:01.335 --> 00:03.337
[♪ theme music playing]

00:28.362 --> 00:30.197
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:33.283 --> 00:34.826
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:34.910 --> 00:36.203
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:37.120 --> 00:39.122
[♪ soft nostalgic music playing]

00:39.206 --> 00:41.208
[ice clinking, crackling]

00:44.294 --> 00:47.214
EPISODE 1

00:48.966 --> 00:50.884
[woman vocalizing tune over speaker phone]

00:50.968 --> 00:52.261
[woman] Hold on. Let me start over.

00:53.553 --> 00:56.723
[woman continues vocalizing]

01:02.271 --> 01:03.730
The song that starts like that.

01:04.314 --> 01:08.443
I heard it a few days ago on the radio,
and they said it helps with insomnia.

01:08.569 --> 01:10.571
You said your sleep pattern
has been off lately.

01:10.654 --> 01:13.115
Try listening to it
when you can't sleep. Okay?

01:18.870 --> 01:20.455
This is Seoul.

01:20.539 --> 01:21.915
Boston, please respond.

01:23.750 --> 01:25.377
Hey, engineering student.

01:28.046 --> 01:29.047
Chan.

01:29.965 --> 01:31.967
Hey, Chan!

01:32.050 --> 01:34.052
[♪ soft music continues]

01:49.693 --> 01:52.863
[in English] Is it a gift?
I could engrave it if you'd like.

01:53.530 --> 01:54.948
[sighs]

02:04.499 --> 02:07.169
[team leader in Korean]
The design contest winner is…

02:07.669 --> 02:08.962
Song Haran!

02:09.838 --> 02:11.632
Me? You're kidding, right?

02:11.715 --> 02:13.216
Well, this is unexpected.

02:13.300 --> 02:14.718
The second-year newbie won.

02:14.801 --> 02:16.094
Congratulations, Haran.

02:16.178 --> 02:17.346
-[woman 1] Congrats, newbie!
-Really?

02:17.429 --> 02:19.264
-[man] Congrats! You deserve it!
-[woman 2] Congratulations!

02:19.348 --> 02:21.016
-[Haran] Thank you!
-[laptop pings]

02:21.099 --> 02:22.559
I can't believe it!

02:22.643 --> 02:23.685
Chan! Chan! Chan!

02:23.769 --> 02:25.103
[laptop pings]

02:25.187 --> 02:27.189
The pen you sent me for my birthday…

02:27.272 --> 02:30.942
I used it to draw a design,
and it won in our company contest!

02:31.026 --> 02:33.862
-Let's go!
-[Chan] It won?

02:33.945 --> 02:35.947
[Haran] Thank you so much!

02:36.823 --> 02:38.241
You know,

02:38.325 --> 02:39.660
you're my savior.

02:51.588 --> 02:53.090
[indistinct chatter]

02:53.173 --> 02:54.257
[phone chimes]

02:56.134 --> 02:57.427
[Haran] Hey, it smells like rain.

02:57.511 --> 02:59.513
[rain pattering]

03:10.524 --> 03:13.193
You know that particular smell
before it rains?

03:13.276 --> 03:15.529
I love that smell.

03:16.279 --> 03:19.783
But it disappears so quickly,
so I just stand there smelling it.

03:20.575 --> 03:23.412
[Chan] That's the smell
of organic matter diffusing.

03:23.495 --> 03:24.579
It's called petrichor,

03:24.663 --> 03:27.124
and it's when plant-derived
organic matter spreads--

03:27.207 --> 03:29.626
-[Haran] Hey, nerd. Stop.
-[Chan] The pores in rock crevices…

03:30.919 --> 03:34.005
[Haran] Stop ruining my joy
with science talk, you nerd.

03:36.675 --> 03:37.676
[chuckles]

03:37.759 --> 03:40.470
[Haran] Anyway, smelling the rain
puts me in a good mood.

03:41.138 --> 03:43.473
You should try it sometime.
I recommend it.

03:48.687 --> 03:53.150
[♪ Baroque music playing, J.S. Bach
"Goldberg Variations, BWV 988: Aria"]

04:32.189 --> 04:35.692
[Haran] But the catch is that
you always end up with a nasty cold.

04:40.071 --> 04:41.740
ACHOO!

04:42.073 --> 04:43.074
[inhales deeply]

04:44.242 --> 04:45.243
[sneezes]

04:45.786 --> 04:47.037
[chuckles]

04:47.913 --> 04:48.914
[sneezes]

04:54.377 --> 04:56.087
Hey, it's a vapor trail.

04:56.671 --> 04:59.674
[groans] I wish I could get on a plane
and go see Chan.

05:00.634 --> 05:02.511
The boyfriend who's studying in Boston?

05:02.594 --> 05:05.722
I heard Chan's too busy with research
to come during vacation.

05:05.806 --> 05:07.849
Eunchan, you know Haran's boyfriend?

05:07.933 --> 05:08.934
A bit.

05:09.017 --> 05:10.143
He's my little brother.

05:10.227 --> 05:12.103
-What?
-Really?

05:12.187 --> 05:16.024
Let's enjoy our four days off
and work hard for our next season.

05:16.107 --> 05:17.359
[employees] Yes, ma'am!

05:17.442 --> 05:18.443
[employees laugh]

05:19.444 --> 05:20.445
Four days?

05:21.613 --> 05:23.782
[cell phone vibrating]

05:23.865 --> 05:25.033
[Haran panting] Hey, Yujeong!

05:25.116 --> 05:26.827
[Yujeong] We're getting together later.
You free?

05:27.410 --> 05:28.662
Why are you running?

05:28.745 --> 05:31.623
I'm going to Boston to meet Chan.

05:32.123 --> 05:33.708
I'll tell you everything later.

05:34.751 --> 05:35.752
[phone beeps]

05:37.003 --> 05:39.005
[birds chirping]

05:48.348 --> 05:49.891
[sighs]

05:57.858 --> 05:58.859
[sighs]

06:07.158 --> 06:08.493
[laptop pings]

06:11.746 --> 06:12.747
Tsk.

06:13.331 --> 06:14.416
[sighs softly]

06:16.918 --> 06:19.254
[Haran] Chan, I saw a vapor trail earlier.

06:19.337 --> 06:21.840
But that made me want
to get on a plane to go see you.

06:21.923 --> 06:23.174
So…

06:23.967 --> 06:27.345
-Ta-da! I'm at the airport!
-[♪ pleasant music playing]

06:27.429 --> 06:28.680
Isn't that crazy?

06:28.763 --> 06:31.099
I'll have to come back
after only a few hours,

06:31.182 --> 06:33.310
but I wanted
to tell you something in person.

06:34.019 --> 06:37.606
I'll be there at about 1:00 p.m.
in Boston, so just hang in there.

06:38.106 --> 06:39.107
Wait.

06:39.858 --> 06:42.944
I changed my mind.
I'm going to say it now. Hang on.

06:45.780 --> 06:47.157
Chan.

06:47.240 --> 06:48.575
I love you.

06:49.826 --> 06:51.453
I love you, Chan. [chuckles]

06:58.960 --> 07:01.087
[ticking]

07:11.806 --> 07:12.807
[in English] BIT, please.

07:26.154 --> 07:28.156
[♪ pleasant music continues]

07:33.828 --> 07:35.413
5 MINUTES, 0.7 MILES

07:35.497 --> 07:37.207
[gasps, in Korean] Just five minutes left.

08:06.027 --> 08:07.028
[student in English] Hey!

08:12.450 --> 08:13.743
[panting]

08:17.747 --> 08:19.666
[♪ mysterious music playing]

08:27.048 --> 08:28.091
[sighs]

08:36.725 --> 08:37.767
[explosion]

08:41.020 --> 08:42.731
[♪ dramatic music playing]

08:42.814 --> 08:43.982
[distant explosion]

08:49.029 --> 08:50.655
[sirens wailing, blaring]

08:52.657 --> 08:54.659
[people clamoring]

09:05.295 --> 09:07.881
[cell phone vibrating]

09:07.964 --> 09:10.759
EUNCHAN

09:10.842 --> 09:11.885
[gasps]

09:13.219 --> 09:14.637
Hello?

09:14.721 --> 09:17.390
[Eunchan] Haran, what do I do?

09:20.852 --> 09:21.978
Chan…

09:23.229 --> 09:24.898
[sobbing] Chan is…

09:24.981 --> 09:26.983
[♪ dramatic music continues]

09:54.969 --> 09:55.970
[shuddering]

09:56.054 --> 09:58.056
[high-pitched ringing]

10:00.475 --> 10:01.518
[groans softly]

10:06.439 --> 10:07.440
[exhales]

10:10.443 --> 10:13.279
-[sirens wailing, blaring]
-[people clamoring]

10:13.363 --> 10:16.116
[♪ somber music playing]

10:48.690 --> 10:51.067
[♪ somber music continuing]

11:11.129 --> 11:14.382
SEOUL, SEVEN YEARS LATER

11:14.883 --> 11:15.884
[camera clicks]

11:15.967 --> 11:17.969
[♪ upbeat electronic music
playing on speakers]

11:21.556 --> 11:22.557
Let's begin.

11:23.308 --> 11:24.309
One, two, three.

11:24.767 --> 11:25.852
[cameras clicking]

11:25.935 --> 11:27.353
Awesome.

11:27.437 --> 11:29.355
-[Hayeong] All right.
-Let's take a few more and call it.

11:29.439 --> 11:30.481
Okay.

11:43.620 --> 11:45.371
Excuse me. Coming through.

11:49.542 --> 11:51.628
-Hi.
-Hey. The outfits…

11:51.711 --> 11:53.713
I like how the texture shows here.

11:53.796 --> 11:55.798
[♪ upbeat music continuing]

11:59.761 --> 12:01.763
[cameras clicking]

12:01.846 --> 12:02.931
Nice.

12:03.014 --> 12:04.891
-Nice! You look great.
-[cameraman] Perfect.

12:04.974 --> 12:07.143
Dart. 0.5.

12:12.065 --> 12:13.775
Ms. Kim is here.

12:14.192 --> 12:15.193
[hiccups]

12:24.494 --> 12:27.372
Let's fix the darts by 0.5 inches
before resuming.

12:27.455 --> 12:29.249
Start pinning right away!

12:32.919 --> 12:34.087
Lights.

12:35.630 --> 12:38.925
Dim the backlight by 10%
and adjust the fill lights.

12:39.008 --> 12:40.093
Everyone, move.

12:40.718 --> 12:42.679
-[staff 1] All right.
-[staff 2] Hurry!

12:43.972 --> 12:45.098
Quickly, everyone!

12:47.767 --> 12:48.935
[camera clicking]

12:49.018 --> 12:50.019
All right.

12:50.895 --> 12:51.938
Two, three.

12:53.439 --> 12:54.440
[in English] Okay.

12:55.400 --> 12:57.527
[in Korean] Okay. Great work, everyone.

12:57.610 --> 12:59.279
-Great work, everyone.
-[applause]

13:01.072 --> 13:03.574
The Korean queen of fashion,

13:04.242 --> 13:06.327
the head of Nana Atelier.

13:06.411 --> 13:08.413
Give a round of applause
to our queen, Nana.

13:08.496 --> 13:09.747
[Nana] It's fine.

13:09.831 --> 13:11.666
Clap for the person in charge, not me.

13:11.749 --> 13:15.253
Ah, the person who oversaw it all,
from the outfits to the shoot.

13:15.336 --> 13:17.964
Let's give a hand
to our lead designer, Song Haran!

13:18.047 --> 13:20.466
[employees cheering, applauding]

13:23.678 --> 13:24.929
Excuse me…

13:25.013 --> 13:27.557
I'm sorry, but I don't think she's here.
[chuckles nervously]

13:28.349 --> 13:29.434
[staff] Where did she go?

13:30.601 --> 13:31.894
-She's not here?
-[exclaims]

13:31.978 --> 13:32.979
What's going on?

13:33.062 --> 13:34.063
She was just here.

13:34.897 --> 13:37.567
She even approved the final select shots.

13:38.109 --> 13:39.110
Ghosting…

13:39.527 --> 13:42.613
[groans] She disappeared again,
like always.

13:43.614 --> 13:44.657
[cell phone chimes]

13:44.741 --> 13:47.785
Ms. Song's routine never changes.
[chuckles]

13:47.869 --> 13:49.162
[chuckles]

13:49.245 --> 13:51.956
She's like my salary.

13:52.040 --> 13:53.249
She disappears every time.

13:53.791 --> 13:55.585
[Seung-gyu] Right. [chuckles]

13:55.668 --> 13:57.670
[silence]

14:06.596 --> 14:10.767
[♪ Baroque music playing, J.S. Bach
"Goldberg Variations, BWV 988: Aria"]

14:23.863 --> 14:24.947
[sighs]

15:03.361 --> 15:04.946
[indistinct announcement on PA]

15:06.656 --> 15:08.616
Mr. Yeon's coming to our hotel.

15:08.699 --> 15:10.785
The car rental…

15:12.036 --> 15:13.037
Where did he go?

15:15.331 --> 15:17.416
[sighs] Did he wander off again?

15:20.503 --> 15:22.755
[man in English]
Do you guys remember what I just told you?

15:22.839 --> 15:23.923
[group] Yeah!

15:24.006 --> 15:25.883
-[man] Okay, let's go.
-[camera whirs]

15:26.551 --> 15:28.261
[camera ticking]

15:28.344 --> 15:30.096
[♪ pleasant music playing]

15:31.472 --> 15:32.849
[in Korean] What's one plus one?

15:32.932 --> 15:35.852
-[group] Two!
-[in English] Two!

15:36.185 --> 15:37.228
[camera clicks]

15:37.311 --> 15:38.312
[camera clicks]

15:38.396 --> 15:40.106
[Chan in Korean] Ben, look.
Didn't it come out nice?

15:40.940 --> 15:43.401
[scoffs] I bet
you're the only one in this world

15:43.484 --> 15:47.572
who always makes friends
with everyone on the plane.

15:47.655 --> 15:48.948
You think so?

15:51.826 --> 15:54.412
Mm! [exclaims]
This taste brings back memories.

15:54.495 --> 15:55.580
[exclaims]

15:57.039 --> 15:58.666
When was the last time you were in Korea?

15:59.250 --> 16:01.335
[inhales sharply]
It's been about seven years.

16:01.419 --> 16:03.504
[Ben] Isn't your family in Korea?

16:03.588 --> 16:04.964
Why didn't you come--

16:05.047 --> 16:07.383
Ben. Let's go to Hangang River
after the meeting.

16:07.466 --> 16:10.386
-[laughs]
-No, wait. Maybe Namsan?

16:10.469 --> 16:11.470
Oh!

16:12.096 --> 16:14.098
[in English] I got a list, man.

16:15.099 --> 16:19.937
[in Korean] Okay. Let's look through
my Seoul destinations list.

16:20.563 --> 16:21.939
-First…
-[exclaiming]

16:22.023 --> 16:23.774
No, I can't hear you! I'm going to sleep.

16:23.858 --> 16:25.151
[exclaiming]

16:25.735 --> 16:27.195
Then, I'll have fun by myself.

16:27.278 --> 16:29.155
-Great. Go do that.
-[chuckles]

16:30.531 --> 16:33.242
[breathes deeply]

16:36.746 --> 16:39.248
[♪ sentimental music playing]

16:39.332 --> 16:40.875
I really did come back.

16:43.502 --> 16:44.545
[window whirring]

16:45.880 --> 16:47.048
[wind whooshing]

17:04.899 --> 17:06.817
[wind whooshing]

17:06.901 --> 17:08.986
-[leaves rustling]
-[birds chirping]

17:09.070 --> 17:11.822
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

17:12.531 --> 17:14.575
Nice to meet you. I'm Yeon Taeseok.

17:14.659 --> 17:16.702
[exclaims] It's nice to meet you,
Mr. Yeon!

17:16.786 --> 17:18.621
I really wanted to see you.

17:18.704 --> 17:20.498
After communicating through just emails,

17:20.581 --> 17:21.707
I knew I'd be happy,

17:21.791 --> 17:23.709
but I can't believe how excited I am.

17:23.793 --> 17:26.545
-Well, I'm not that excited…
-[♪ happy music playing]

17:26.629 --> 17:28.464
Just think of him

17:28.547 --> 17:30.967
like a golden retriever
who loves people. [chuckles]

17:31.050 --> 17:32.885
I see. A golden retriever.

17:33.594 --> 17:34.929
But your Korean is really…

17:35.012 --> 17:36.722
Ah. I'm Ben.

17:36.806 --> 17:40.142
My wife's Korean,
and my in-laws live in Pangyo.

17:40.226 --> 17:42.019
-Ah. Right. Ben.
-[Ben] Yes.

17:42.103 --> 17:43.229
[claps]

17:43.312 --> 17:45.481
Stand over here, Ben.

17:45.565 --> 17:46.857
Let me formally introduce myself.

17:47.650 --> 17:49.277
I'm the one who proposed this project

17:50.027 --> 17:52.697
and a supervisor
with CAN Animation Studio, Seon…

17:54.073 --> 17:58.578
Well, many people get confused,
so let me tell you in advance.

17:58.661 --> 18:01.038
My name's Seonu Chan, not Seon Uchan.

18:02.373 --> 18:03.958
-[Remy] This too?
-[Hayeong] Mmm-hmm.

18:04.667 --> 18:07.003
Wait. Hang on. I can't carry this alone.

18:07.086 --> 18:08.629
[in English] You can do it, baby.

18:08.713 --> 18:11.549
-[staff 1 in Korean] Great work, guys.
-[staff 2] Great job.

18:11.632 --> 18:14.343
-[staff 3] Great work, everyone.
-[staff 4] Good job.

18:14.427 --> 18:17.346
After checking if we have everything,
let's clean up and go.

18:17.430 --> 18:20.182
We should go now
if we want to make it to the afterparty.

18:20.266 --> 18:21.267
[Sol] What's going on?

18:21.976 --> 18:24.478
I guess Ms. Song didn't arrive first.

18:24.562 --> 18:26.856
-I should text her to come to the party.
-[Remy in English] Stop!

18:26.939 --> 18:29.025
[in Korean] Sol, our rookie intern.

18:29.650 --> 18:31.110
You're still clueless about her.

18:31.902 --> 18:35.156
Honey, have you ever had lunch
with Ms. Song before?

18:35.239 --> 18:37.533
-Yes or no?
-No, never.

18:38.242 --> 18:41.996
She always leaves first during lunchtime,
so she must be busy meeting people.

18:42.079 --> 18:45.333
-Not at all.
-Every day, all the time.

18:45.416 --> 18:48.085
Do you think it makes sense
to always have plans?

18:48.169 --> 18:51.714
Gosh. Are you saying
she's avoiding us on purpose?

18:51.797 --> 18:53.466
That's right. [chuckles]

18:53.549 --> 18:56.886
She loves to brood on her own.

18:56.969 --> 18:58.679
She really isn't my vibe.

18:58.763 --> 19:01.932
[sighs] Where is she
always disappearing to?

19:06.062 --> 19:08.356
[♪ serene music playing on speakers]

19:12.985 --> 19:14.487
[sighs contentedly]

19:19.075 --> 19:20.701
PARK GENIUS

19:46.185 --> 19:48.771
-[automation in English] Two points.
-[exclaims]

19:49.146 --> 19:50.147
Three points.

19:50.231 --> 19:51.357
[game buzzes]

19:51.440 --> 19:52.441
-Three points.
-[exclaims]

19:52.525 --> 19:54.026
-[♪ lighthearted music playing]
-[arcade sounds]

19:54.110 --> 19:55.194
[exclaims]

19:55.277 --> 19:56.362
-[camera clicks]
-[in Korean] I got it!

20:00.074 --> 20:01.826
It looks so good.

20:02.993 --> 20:04.078
Mmm.

20:05.705 --> 20:07.206
CHAN SENT PHOTOS

20:07.289 --> 20:09.417
-[cell phone pinging]
-[groans]

20:09.500 --> 20:12.002
[sighing]

20:13.087 --> 20:14.130
[pinging stops]

20:18.551 --> 20:20.219
[in English] Oh, God.

20:20.302 --> 20:21.470
[sighs]

20:21.554 --> 20:24.306
[in Korean] What sort of Korean
enjoys Korea this much?

20:25.099 --> 20:26.851
[♪ lighthearted music continues]

20:28.894 --> 20:29.979
[camera clicks]

20:44.076 --> 20:46.078
[♪ serene music playing on speakers]

20:48.789 --> 20:50.458
[machine thudding loudly]

20:59.800 --> 21:01.135
Sorry about that.

21:02.052 --> 21:05.556
The ice machine
is acting up today. [chuckles]

21:06.056 --> 21:07.224
Be quiet.

21:09.727 --> 21:10.728
Quiet!

21:12.313 --> 21:14.482
Good boy. [chuckles]

21:14.565 --> 21:15.858
This is AI.

21:16.650 --> 21:17.902
[chuckles]

21:18.986 --> 21:20.112
Oh, those.

21:20.196 --> 21:22.239
If you're interested, check them out.

21:22.323 --> 21:25.284
One of my regulars here
organized an exhibit,

21:25.367 --> 21:28.746
and they're showing paintings
for each season.

21:28.829 --> 21:31.499
You can take a bunch of those
and go with friends.

21:31.582 --> 21:34.210
One is enough. Thank you.

21:34.293 --> 21:35.920
Ah. Really?

21:38.172 --> 21:40.049
Going by yourself will be nice, too.

21:41.967 --> 21:45.137
RADIANT SEASONS

21:45.221 --> 21:46.806
[♪ pleasant music playing]

21:48.766 --> 21:51.602
[receptionist] Proceed through
the four seasonal rooms in order.

21:51.685 --> 21:52.686
Okay.

21:54.897 --> 21:57.942
"SHIM"
Coffee House

21:59.944 --> 22:02.363
SPRING ROOM, THE WONDER OF LIFE

22:17.294 --> 22:19.880
WINTER ROOM, DEEP SILENCE

22:19.964 --> 22:20.965
[music fades]

22:26.136 --> 22:28.055
[footsteps]

22:34.270 --> 22:35.312
[clicks]

22:37.189 --> 22:38.190
[chuckles softly]

22:43.904 --> 22:44.905
[clicks]

22:48.826 --> 22:50.244
[guide on headphones] A lone woman

22:50.327 --> 22:53.330
stands with her back turned
in a white, snowy landscape,

22:54.081 --> 22:57.084
quietly conveying
a sense of sorrow and emptiness.

22:59.461 --> 23:02.047
Rather than sharp tension,
the artist's brush captures

23:02.756 --> 23:06.260
the gentle air
and subtle tremble of light.

23:06.343 --> 23:08.345
[♪ soft emotional song playing]

23:15.436 --> 23:18.230
No way…

23:46.175 --> 23:47.176
[Haran] Chan.

23:47.927 --> 23:49.094
I love you, Chan.

23:50.679 --> 23:53.140
[♪ soft emotional song continuing]

24:01.398 --> 24:02.399
[Chan exclaims]

24:04.443 --> 24:05.444
I'm sorry.

24:18.165 --> 24:20.125
[panting]

24:26.715 --> 24:29.134
You idiot.
What will you do if it really is her?

24:32.680 --> 24:33.681
[song fades]

24:35.516 --> 24:37.518
[♪ soft surreal music playing]

25:01.417 --> 25:02.418
[music fades]

25:04.461 --> 25:06.130
[hammering echoes]

25:06.213 --> 25:08.799
[saw whirring]

25:10.801 --> 25:13.303
-[rattling]
-[♪ tense music playing]

25:13.387 --> 25:15.055
-[wood clanks]
-Huh?

25:17.141 --> 25:18.392
Hey, watch out.

25:21.812 --> 25:23.397
-[metal creaks]
-Watch out!

25:24.606 --> 25:26.025
Song Haran!

25:32.072 --> 25:34.033
-[crashing]
-[women scream]

25:37.036 --> 25:39.621
-[exclaims] Are you okay?
-[frantic chatter]

25:39.705 --> 25:40.873
That was close.

25:40.956 --> 25:42.583
-Are you all right?
-[women gasp]

25:42.666 --> 25:44.626
-[woman] Gosh. That was close.
-[breathing shakily]

25:44.710 --> 25:46.295
[man] Are you okay?

25:46.378 --> 25:48.422
[woman] Should we call emergency services?

25:48.505 --> 25:49.757
[man] Are you all right?

25:49.840 --> 25:51.175
-[woman] Are you okay?
-[man] Are you okay?

25:51.258 --> 25:52.926
-Come quickly!
-[Haran] Yes, I'm okay.

25:53.010 --> 25:54.261
-[woman] Are you okay?
-[man] Is anyone hurt?

25:54.344 --> 25:55.721
[man 2] Get down here!

25:55.804 --> 25:57.222
-[man 1] Are they okay?
-[man 2] It's dangerous.

25:57.306 --> 25:58.474
You should all come down.

25:58.557 --> 26:00.017
-[woman] That was so close.
-[man] Come on.

26:01.477 --> 26:03.479
[♪ pleasant music playing]

26:04.646 --> 26:06.231
[Ben on phone] Hey, Too Much.

26:06.315 --> 26:09.276
Why is a Korean so busy touring Seoul?

26:09.359 --> 26:10.402
Right?

26:11.070 --> 26:12.988
Maybe I overdid it.

26:14.782 --> 26:16.992
I fled seven years ago

26:18.202 --> 26:20.913
because I thought I'd see her
everywhere I went.

26:21.872 --> 26:24.041
Seoul seems so big,

26:24.708 --> 26:27.419
but it was actually really small.

26:27.503 --> 26:29.296
Are you saying it's big or small?

26:31.090 --> 26:32.091
Hey, Chan.

26:33.300 --> 26:34.802
Did something happen?

26:36.011 --> 26:37.471
Mmm…

26:40.307 --> 26:42.309
Something did happen…

26:43.185 --> 26:44.186
[chuckles]

26:45.813 --> 26:47.523
but I'm going to pretend it didn't.

26:49.024 --> 26:52.236
I'll think about this today
and forget about it tomorrow,

26:52.319 --> 26:54.571
so don't worry and go to bed.

26:54.655 --> 26:55.781
Bye.

26:56.949 --> 26:58.534
[phone clicks, beeps]

27:01.745 --> 27:02.746
[smacks lips]

27:07.167 --> 27:08.252
[sighs]

27:09.586 --> 27:10.796
[pen scratching]

27:16.885 --> 27:19.513
RADIANT SEASONS

27:19.596 --> 27:21.765
[♪ mysterious music playing]

27:21.849 --> 27:22.850
[Chan] Song Haran!

27:23.809 --> 27:25.435
-[crashes]
-[women scream]

27:26.979 --> 27:29.314
I'm sure they called my name.

27:30.691 --> 27:31.817
Who was it?

27:34.653 --> 27:38.991
Of the three, I'm in charge of designing
and planning the Korean character… [sighs]

27:39.074 --> 27:40.784
CHARACTERS
NIA, WON, FIN

27:40.868 --> 27:44.580
[inhales sharply] Just think of me
as the guy in charge of Won.

27:45.414 --> 27:47.708
[Ben] To highlight the identities
of each character,

27:47.791 --> 27:50.961
we planned collaborations
with designers from each country.

27:51.545 --> 27:53.297
[Chan] I made the collaboration offer

27:53.380 --> 27:57.843
because I really wanted you
to design the Korean character's outfits.

27:59.177 --> 28:00.429
What do you think, Ms. Kim?

28:05.976 --> 28:06.977
Ms. Kim?

28:09.479 --> 28:11.940
So why should I do this?

28:13.317 --> 28:14.610
[Chan] I was curious.

28:15.152 --> 28:17.905
To be honest, I was excited.

28:17.988 --> 28:21.241
I thought your roots
were similar to Won's.

28:22.117 --> 28:25.787
Won isn't someone who shines like the sun.

28:25.871 --> 28:28.790
Instead, she gives light

28:28.874 --> 28:30.876
to those in the darkness,

28:31.752 --> 28:32.753
like the moon.

28:33.378 --> 28:35.047
"Douceur lunaire."

28:35.797 --> 28:37.799
[♪ pleasant music playing]

28:38.425 --> 28:39.426
[mouthing] What's that?

28:40.510 --> 28:42.054
"Soft moonlight."

28:42.137 --> 28:44.681
The first collection you put out
when you were 22.

28:44.765 --> 28:46.266
I saw it myself.

28:47.392 --> 28:51.021
You reinterpreted Korean traditional silk
through moonlight.

28:52.981 --> 28:55.192
You saw it yourself?

28:55.275 --> 28:58.111
It was on display at the fashion school
you attended in France.

28:59.696 --> 29:01.782
Thanks to you,

29:03.075 --> 29:04.785
I got to see the Eiffel Tower, too.

29:07.955 --> 29:12.084
So, what if you expressed Won
with roots like that?

29:12.167 --> 29:13.251
[exclaims]

29:13.335 --> 29:17.172
Just imagining that made me so excited.

29:26.306 --> 29:27.307
So?

29:29.059 --> 29:30.143
What should we do first?

29:32.270 --> 29:33.563
[in English] Yes!

29:34.856 --> 29:35.857
[mouthing] Unbelievable.

29:36.400 --> 29:39.152
Then, let's take a selfie first
to celebrate this day.

29:39.861 --> 29:42.030
Sorry, but you really shouldn't…

29:43.740 --> 29:45.993
Was I being rude, by any chance?

29:46.618 --> 29:47.619
Very rude.

29:51.164 --> 29:52.249
You know,

29:54.292 --> 29:55.711
my left side is prettier.

29:58.547 --> 30:01.425
Then, I'll take one from the left.

30:01.508 --> 30:03.760
One, two, three.

30:03.844 --> 30:05.053
[camera clicks]

30:08.890 --> 30:11.768
Should we show you the story reel first?

30:11.852 --> 30:14.312
-The video will be pretty helpful.
-Sure.

30:14.396 --> 30:16.815
The USB is in my car,
so I'll go and get it.

30:21.611 --> 30:22.779
[door closes]

30:22.863 --> 30:23.864
CHARACTER "WON"

30:23.947 --> 30:25.115
[Nana] It's strange.

30:25.699 --> 30:27.409
-She looks familiar.
-[Ben] Pardon?

30:27.492 --> 30:30.370
It's an original character
that Chan created.

30:30.454 --> 30:31.455
No…

30:32.414 --> 30:34.124
I'm sure I've seen that face before.

30:34.207 --> 30:35.208
[elevator dings]

30:38.462 --> 30:39.796
[humming]

30:42.674 --> 30:44.217
[humming continues]

30:50.140 --> 30:51.141
Hmm?

31:03.612 --> 31:05.113
[sighs]

31:08.742 --> 31:10.744
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

31:30.013 --> 31:31.014
Huh.

31:31.807 --> 31:33.809
[footsteps echoing]

32:00.502 --> 32:01.753
[Nana] Ms. Song.

32:01.837 --> 32:02.921
Right.

32:03.004 --> 32:06.508
This character looks like
our lead designer, Song Haran.

32:08.176 --> 32:09.761
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

32:19.396 --> 32:20.397
[echoing] I'm sorry.

32:21.064 --> 32:23.275
I dropped my pen by accident.

32:29.739 --> 32:31.116
May I help you?

32:33.451 --> 32:34.452
[echoing stops]

32:34.536 --> 32:36.580
Are you here for the collaboration?

32:39.457 --> 32:40.458
No…

32:42.961 --> 32:44.171
Oh.

32:44.963 --> 32:45.964
Yes, I am.

32:48.633 --> 32:49.968
It's nice to meet you.

32:50.719 --> 32:52.220
I'm Song Haran, the lead designer.

32:53.096 --> 32:54.097
[sighs]

32:54.848 --> 32:55.974
[mutters] "It's nice to meet you"?

32:58.476 --> 33:00.770
-Excuse me?
-Right.

33:02.856 --> 33:04.983
It's nice to meet you.

33:08.653 --> 33:09.988
I'm Seonu Chan.

33:10.071 --> 33:12.073
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

33:16.995 --> 33:18.038
My pen…

33:18.872 --> 33:20.373
Ah… Here.

33:23.168 --> 33:24.419
Thank you.

33:34.221 --> 33:35.680
Do you have something to say?

33:37.140 --> 33:38.141
No.

34:03.708 --> 34:06.753
[breathing heavily]

34:12.759 --> 34:14.094
[sighs]

34:14.177 --> 34:16.763
NANA ATELIER DESIGNERS
LEAD DESIGNER SONG HARAN

34:20.392 --> 34:21.810
[sighs]

34:34.114 --> 34:35.323
Hey, Chan.

34:35.407 --> 34:37.909
-What happened to you?
-It's fine.

34:38.493 --> 34:39.494
[knock on door]

34:42.872 --> 34:43.873
[door closes]

34:45.000 --> 34:46.001
[Haran] I'm sorry.

34:46.084 --> 34:47.919
My prior engagement
ran longer than expected.

34:48.003 --> 34:49.129
No need for excuses.

34:49.713 --> 34:50.755
Say hello.

34:50.839 --> 34:52.340
This is Lead Designer Song Haran,

34:52.424 --> 34:55.260
who will be the main support
for this collaboration project.

34:55.343 --> 34:57.804
She'll be working with you
for the entire three months.

34:58.888 --> 35:00.015
Let's continue.

35:00.098 --> 35:02.183
[Ben] Then,
let's watch the story reel together.

35:03.018 --> 35:04.227
[Nana] Wait.

35:05.270 --> 35:06.938
Mr. Seonu.

35:07.564 --> 35:08.982
That character.

35:09.524 --> 35:10.734
Was it based on someone?

35:12.485 --> 35:14.988
No, it just came to mind.

35:15.071 --> 35:16.323
My grandmother…

35:16.406 --> 35:19.451
I mean, Ms. Kim said that
Won resembles my sister…

35:19.534 --> 35:20.660
[groans]

35:20.744 --> 35:23.330
I mean, Lead Designer Song Haran.

35:23.413 --> 35:24.623
[both exclaim]

35:24.706 --> 35:26.082
-Ooh!
-[in English] Oops.

35:26.166 --> 35:27.876
[in Korean] I'm so sorry. I'm so sorry.

35:28.960 --> 35:29.961
I…

35:31.713 --> 35:33.089
I can't stand those messy clothes.

35:33.173 --> 35:35.383
-Remy, get him a new shirt.
-[Remy] Yes, ma'am.

35:35.467 --> 35:36.926
We'll resume in 10 minutes.

35:37.552 --> 35:39.554
[Remy] Why don't you wait
in the fitting room?

35:39.638 --> 35:41.806
I'll pick out a pretty shirt for you.

35:42.265 --> 35:43.433
It's on the fourth floor.

35:43.516 --> 35:45.226
-[Chan] I'll do it.
-[Hayeong] No, it's fine.

35:45.310 --> 35:47.395
It's all right.
Just head to the fourth floor.

35:55.070 --> 35:56.946
-[sighs]
-[footsteps approaching]

36:03.703 --> 36:06.706
Can you deliver this to the animator?
[chuckles]

36:06.790 --> 36:11.586
I mean, seeing you
brooding like this by yourself again…

36:11.670 --> 36:15.882
You look [in English] very, very…
[in Korean] free right now. [chuckles]

36:18.051 --> 36:19.052
[Remy chuckles]

36:24.808 --> 36:25.809
[sighs]

36:25.892 --> 36:27.394
[sighs heavily]

36:27.477 --> 36:29.479
[♪ soft pensive music playing]

36:46.746 --> 36:48.498
I'll leave your shirt here.

36:56.256 --> 36:57.549
-[exclaims]
-[groans]

36:57.632 --> 36:59.134
I'm sorry! You weren't answering.

36:59.217 --> 37:00.427
Right.

37:01.970 --> 37:03.513
[sighs] Ah…

37:05.473 --> 37:07.559
Here's your shirt.

37:07.642 --> 37:08.685
Thank you.

37:13.732 --> 37:16.317
[sighing]

37:16.401 --> 37:18.361
[♪ soft pensive music continuing]

37:21.489 --> 37:22.615
[door closes]

37:28.955 --> 37:29.956
What's with you today?

37:31.124 --> 37:32.375
You've been acting weird…

37:33.543 --> 37:34.544
What are you doing?

37:35.086 --> 37:38.047
I'm sorry, Ben.
I'm stepping out of this project.

37:38.882 --> 37:40.091
[exclaims in English] What?

37:40.175 --> 37:41.718
[in Korean] You stick to the schedule.

37:41.801 --> 37:42.844
I'll head back to the US.

37:46.806 --> 37:48.600
This isn't funny, Chan.

37:49.642 --> 37:52.353
I'll call you as soon as I find
a replacement supervisor.

37:54.022 --> 37:55.231
What on earth…

37:55.315 --> 37:56.983
[in English] Are you serious right now?

37:57.066 --> 38:00.153
You know the director's coming here
with the EA team soon, right?

38:00.236 --> 38:03.031
Hundreds of people have been working
on this project for years

38:03.114 --> 38:04.449
because they believed in you.

38:04.532 --> 38:06.451
Not to mention the expenses.

38:07.118 --> 38:08.536
[in Korean] Seonu Chan.

38:10.079 --> 38:12.332
The Seonu Chan I know wouldn't do this.

38:13.082 --> 38:14.250
No, he can't.

38:15.752 --> 38:16.753
Tell me the reason.

38:16.836 --> 38:18.838
[♪ tense music playing]

38:19.839 --> 38:21.007
Because I'm scared.

38:21.090 --> 38:22.175
I shouldn't be here.

38:23.593 --> 38:24.844
What do you mean?

38:26.554 --> 38:28.264
[in English] Sorry, Ben. Not now.

38:29.140 --> 38:30.558
Let's talk about it later, man.

38:39.150 --> 38:42.487
[in Korean] You said
drawing made you so happy.

38:43.446 --> 38:44.989
When you became a supervisor,

38:45.073 --> 38:47.575
you asked me to smack you
because it felt like a dream.

38:48.535 --> 38:50.912
[in English] Now I see
just how little it really means to you.

38:53.915 --> 38:54.916
[in Korean] Fine. Go.

38:55.458 --> 38:58.670
I don't need a supervisor
who gives up so easily on his work.

39:04.717 --> 39:06.219
[door opens, closes]

39:07.971 --> 39:09.013
[sighs]

39:09.097 --> 39:10.682
WON COSTUME COLLABORATION PROPOSAL

39:13.184 --> 39:14.227
[sighs]

39:15.854 --> 39:16.855
[sighs]

39:26.906 --> 39:28.116
[sighs heavily]

39:34.622 --> 39:35.665
Memento mori…

39:43.089 --> 39:44.090
[sighs heavily]

39:54.350 --> 39:55.810
[ticking]

40:00.023 --> 40:01.441
[in English] He sure left quick.

40:02.108 --> 40:04.110
[cell phone vibrating]

40:05.904 --> 40:07.780
Morning, Ben. How are you?

40:07.864 --> 40:10.450
Wait, actually. It's probably
nighttime there, right?

40:10.533 --> 40:12.243
-[chuckles]
-Anyway, I was just wondering

40:12.327 --> 40:14.871
how the first meeting went
for the fashion collaboration.

40:14.954 --> 40:17.457
Uh, yeah, it went well, but…

40:17.540 --> 40:23.129
Before we get into that,
there's been a bit of an issue with Chan.

40:23.212 --> 40:26.382
-Um…
-Hey, am I late?

40:27.592 --> 40:29.969
Sorry. I was taking a shower.

40:31.429 --> 40:33.806
I thought I should get dressed
before hopping on.

40:36.267 --> 40:37.685
Let's share it.

40:38.186 --> 40:39.896
-Okay.
-[Chan sighs]

40:41.481 --> 40:43.358
Okay, um…

40:43.441 --> 40:45.360
I've sent the materials to Ms. Kim,

40:45.443 --> 40:50.073
and we're meeting in a couple of days
to discuss the concept.

40:50.156 --> 40:51.532
[director] All right. Sounds great.

40:51.616 --> 40:54.619
-Right?
-Yeah. Yeah. That's right. Uh…

40:56.496 --> 40:57.956
-[in Korean] Seonu Chan.
-Yeah?

40:58.039 --> 40:59.624
-What was that?
-What?

40:59.707 --> 41:00.792
Your clothes were gone.

41:00.875 --> 41:02.919
Oh. I dropped them off at the cleaners.

41:03.711 --> 41:05.004
They were all crumpled.

41:05.546 --> 41:08.174
-Let's go get some soy-marinated crabs.
-Soy-marinated crabs?

41:08.716 --> 41:09.842
It's midnight.

41:10.176 --> 41:11.761
[sighs]

41:11.844 --> 41:14.389
Don't you know shops are open
24 hours a day in Korea?

41:15.223 --> 41:18.935
We need to eat well
in order to work hard, you know.

41:19.018 --> 41:21.437
-Right, Producer Ben?
-Seonu Chan.

41:22.689 --> 41:25.400
-You're buying.
-No, I'm not. Last one out is buying.

41:27.777 --> 41:28.861
[Ben exclaims]

41:29.946 --> 41:31.948
[door opens, closes]

41:36.577 --> 41:37.912
[sighs]

41:38.538 --> 41:39.789
[♪ pensive music playing]

41:39.872 --> 41:40.873
[clicks tongue]

41:40.957 --> 41:42.250
Three months…

41:43.751 --> 41:45.044
Just three months.

41:49.507 --> 41:51.884
[sighs] I'm sure nothing will happen.

41:56.681 --> 41:57.682
[door opens]

41:58.391 --> 41:59.392
[door closes]

41:59.475 --> 42:01.227
-[wind whooshes]
-[papers rustling]

42:08.067 --> 42:09.402
[camera whirring, clicking]

42:09.485 --> 42:11.487
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

42:14.323 --> 42:16.367
[camera clicking, whirring]

42:22.415 --> 42:23.958
[thudding]

42:24.500 --> 42:27.295
-[door opens, closes]
-[Hadam] Grandma.

42:27.378 --> 42:29.964
-[Nana] Hey.
-I'm here.

42:30.048 --> 42:32.175
How was your day?

42:32.258 --> 42:34.052
Mmm. It was tough.

42:34.135 --> 42:37.263
It's hard being a high school senior.

42:38.097 --> 42:39.432
But…

42:41.768 --> 42:43.102
Ta-da!

42:43.186 --> 42:45.271
I got a perfect score
after all that studying.

42:46.272 --> 42:49.901
Gosh, you did a great job. [chuckles]

42:49.984 --> 42:51.986
These brains and these looks.

42:52.070 --> 42:55.364
I got so many good genes
from you, Grandma.

42:55.448 --> 42:56.657
[Nana chuckles]

42:57.533 --> 43:00.286
But what did I say
was just as important as studying?

43:00.369 --> 43:01.829
Managing my health.

43:02.455 --> 43:03.456
Here.

43:03.956 --> 43:08.002
I've been taking the tonics
that Mr. Yeon gave me to help me focus.

43:08.086 --> 43:09.796
-[chuckles]
-I'll go get some rest.

43:09.879 --> 43:11.380
Good night, Grandma.

43:12.173 --> 43:13.174
Good night.

43:16.344 --> 43:17.512
[sighs]

43:27.605 --> 43:29.607
How are you busier
than a high school senior?

43:32.276 --> 43:33.861
Where on earth have you…

43:36.114 --> 43:37.657
Forget it. Go upstairs.

43:39.158 --> 43:40.159
Good night.

43:47.750 --> 43:48.835
[sighs]

43:52.296 --> 43:53.297
[knock on door]

43:57.343 --> 44:00.179
Why leave your perfectly fine room
and go into that cave?

44:02.598 --> 44:03.599
Come to my study.

44:04.100 --> 44:05.101
What?

44:05.184 --> 44:06.727
Don't make me repeat myself.

44:06.811 --> 44:08.062
Meet Photographer Yoon.

44:08.896 --> 44:10.982
He's been interested in you
for a long time.

44:11.065 --> 44:13.151
He's talented and has great character.

44:13.234 --> 44:15.319
Someone like that is rare.
Give him a chance.

44:15.403 --> 44:18.531
-No, I'm not interested in dating--
-I know.

44:19.031 --> 44:20.241
Just change your mind.

44:21.033 --> 44:23.244
I'll set a date, so meet with him.

44:26.831 --> 44:27.832
[sighs]

44:29.250 --> 44:30.293
I'm sorry.

44:31.669 --> 44:34.505
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

45:02.950 --> 45:05.244
FAREWELL TO MY FORMER LIFE

45:09.916 --> 45:11.542
[♪ soft emotional music continuing]

45:16.672 --> 45:17.798
[sighs]

45:18.799 --> 45:21.344
-[wind whooshing]
-[birds chirping]

45:25.306 --> 45:27.099
[footsteps approaching]

45:29.018 --> 45:30.019
[grunts]

45:32.730 --> 45:34.482
Good morning.

45:34.565 --> 45:36.025
"Good morning"?

45:36.108 --> 45:37.652
When did you get home last night?

45:37.735 --> 45:40.279
Just a little after midnight.

45:40.363 --> 45:42.365
I suddenly got a bunch of plans.

45:43.741 --> 45:47.411
[sighs] Why is everyone
in this household so extreme?

45:47.495 --> 45:49.288
I wish I could mix the two of you.

45:49.372 --> 45:52.250
-What? Me and who?
-[sighs]

45:52.333 --> 45:53.417
[snores]

45:53.501 --> 45:55.419
My lonely eldest sister?

45:56.504 --> 45:57.588
[Hayeong scoffs]

45:57.672 --> 46:00.216
[reporter]
At a construction site in Seoul,

46:00.299 --> 46:02.760
a large tower of scaffolding

46:02.843 --> 46:04.929
begins to tilt toward the sidewalk.

46:05.012 --> 46:09.475
The scaffolding was a second away
from falling on a woman passing by.

46:09.558 --> 46:10.977
[♪ amusing music playing]

46:11.060 --> 46:12.770
What's with all this fuss again?

46:12.853 --> 46:14.647
[reporter continues speaking]

46:14.730 --> 46:15.731
[TV beeps]

46:16.816 --> 46:18.025
What are you doing?

46:18.109 --> 46:19.110
Well…

46:19.527 --> 46:20.569
[sighs]

46:21.404 --> 46:23.781
I'm trying to protect

46:23.864 --> 46:27.994
my beautiful grandmother's skin
from all the electromagnetic waves.

46:28.077 --> 46:31.330
It's a display of touching devotion
from your second granddaughter.

46:31.414 --> 46:35.543
[chuckles nervously]
I'll go get ready for work now.

46:37.795 --> 46:39.630
-[thuds]
-[groans]

46:44.343 --> 46:46.304
She still hasn't sobered up yet.

46:46.387 --> 46:47.805
Haran!

46:48.848 --> 46:50.433
What? Where is she?

46:51.475 --> 46:52.518
Are you in there again?

46:52.601 --> 46:54.812
Come out here right now!

46:56.522 --> 46:57.523
What is it?

46:58.065 --> 46:59.108
[whooshes]

47:03.696 --> 47:04.697
What?

47:06.407 --> 47:10.328
This woman passing by who almost
got hurt at a construction site.

47:10.411 --> 47:11.662
This is you, isn't it?

47:12.038 --> 47:13.039
It is.

47:14.123 --> 47:16.208
-[grumbles]
-What?

47:16.292 --> 47:20.171
Even I was startled by this.
What if Grandma had seen this?

47:20.254 --> 47:24.759
Please, keep your head on straight
when you're outside. Okay?

47:24.842 --> 47:25.926
I'll keep that in mind.

47:27.595 --> 47:29.305
[Hayeong sighs]

47:29.388 --> 47:31.557
[reporter on phone]
The woman stopped just in time

47:31.640 --> 47:33.225
when someone urgently called her name.

47:37.063 --> 47:38.773
Fortunately, that stopped

47:38.856 --> 47:40.441
-what could've been a terrible…
-Hang on.

47:42.777 --> 47:43.778
What?

47:44.236 --> 47:45.237
This shirt…

47:45.321 --> 47:46.822
[both exclaim]

47:46.906 --> 47:48.616
I'm so sorry. I'm so sorry.

47:49.700 --> 47:52.870
Wow. If it weren't for him,
you would've been a goner.

47:53.579 --> 47:56.582
-Hmm? That shirt…
-You recognize it too, right?

47:56.665 --> 48:00.795
Yeah. We remember every color
and texture that people wear.

48:00.878 --> 48:01.879
Isn't that…

48:02.380 --> 48:04.048
the animator's shirt?

48:04.131 --> 48:06.592
-It is. He wore it at the meeting.
-What on earth?

48:06.675 --> 48:09.470
Then, does that mean he was passing by

48:09.553 --> 48:11.597
and shouted when he saw
that you were in danger?

48:11.680 --> 48:13.391
He called out my name.

48:13.474 --> 48:15.184
That's before we even met.

48:15.267 --> 48:18.938
What? How did he call you by your name
when he doesn't know it?

48:20.439 --> 48:22.983
Ah. I get it.

48:23.067 --> 48:25.778
He must be someone in the industry
who knows you.

48:26.779 --> 48:28.197
You're known for your looks.

48:28.280 --> 48:31.158
Plus, plenty of people
wear the same clothes.

48:31.742 --> 48:32.785
You think so?

48:32.868 --> 48:34.870
That's the only way it makes sense.

48:36.372 --> 48:38.916
So who could this savior be?

48:39.875 --> 48:40.876
Right?

48:41.502 --> 48:42.670
Who could it be?

48:46.966 --> 48:48.509
[Sol] Oh. Hello, Ms. Song.

48:49.260 --> 48:50.261
[Seung-gyu] Good morning.

48:50.344 --> 48:51.720
-[in English] Hi.
-[Remy in Korean] Hello.

48:58.144 --> 48:59.145
[beeps]

48:59.979 --> 49:01.105
[knock on door]

49:01.188 --> 49:02.481
Yes?

49:02.565 --> 49:05.568
Ms. Song, the black dress sample is here.

49:09.155 --> 49:10.489
The measurements are perfect.

49:10.573 --> 49:11.949
Let's see it on a mannequin…

49:12.032 --> 49:13.117
I'll wear it.

49:13.200 --> 49:14.994
That will be easier to check.

49:15.077 --> 49:16.704
-Okay. Thanks.
-No problem.

49:19.790 --> 49:21.792
WORK ORDER

49:22.543 --> 49:23.544
Oh?

49:25.671 --> 49:27.006
Ms. Song.

49:27.089 --> 49:28.632
What's with this men's shirt?

49:28.716 --> 49:31.093
Just give that to me
and change into the dress.

49:31.177 --> 49:32.178
[Sol] Okay.

49:34.513 --> 49:35.931
[door closes]

49:36.015 --> 49:38.017
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

49:41.854 --> 49:44.773
[sighs] I'm sure it's the same shirt.

49:47.234 --> 49:49.487
[Hayeong] Plenty of people
wear the same clothes.

49:51.405 --> 49:52.531
[sighs]

50:03.542 --> 50:04.543
The art exhibit.

50:04.627 --> 50:06.295
RADIANT SEASONS

50:06.378 --> 50:09.965
I went to the exhibit
on the day of our lookbook shoot…

50:12.343 --> 50:13.344
It was the 16th.

50:14.845 --> 50:17.556
He was at the exhibit
on the same day as me.

50:18.307 --> 50:19.308
Then…

50:19.892 --> 50:21.977
he really was the one who called my name?

50:22.770 --> 50:25.689
SEONU CHAN

50:26.649 --> 50:28.108
Seonu Chan.

50:29.735 --> 50:30.986
Seonu Chan…

50:31.070 --> 50:33.239
[♪ suspenseful music continuing]

50:33.322 --> 50:34.573
[sighs]

50:36.825 --> 50:38.494
It doesn't ring a bell.

50:39.620 --> 50:41.956
How did he know my name?

50:46.669 --> 50:47.711
[sighs]

50:47.795 --> 50:50.089
SEONU CHAN

50:50.172 --> 50:51.674
[ice crackling]

50:55.761 --> 50:57.179
[Haran] It's nice to meet you.

50:57.263 --> 50:59.848
I'm Song Haran, the lead designer.

51:03.477 --> 51:06.021
Chan. Chan.

51:06.105 --> 51:07.356
I love you.

51:07.439 --> 51:09.024
I love you, Chan.

51:09.108 --> 51:10.943
[EKG beeping]

51:12.444 --> 51:13.487
[explosion]

51:13.571 --> 51:14.697
[gasps]

51:15.322 --> 51:17.324
[♪ soft pensive music playing]

51:17.408 --> 51:19.994
[breathing heavily]

51:34.300 --> 51:35.384
[sighs]

51:41.974 --> 51:43.809
[Remy screams]

51:43.892 --> 51:45.436
[Sol] Ms. Song.

51:45.519 --> 51:48.063
-Something weird was delivered to you.
-What a nutjob.

51:49.815 --> 51:53.360
What are you going to do?
I'm the one who received this delivery.

51:53.444 --> 51:54.820
I'm going to be traumatized

51:54.903 --> 51:57.573
after seeing something that sickening
with my pretty eyes.

51:57.656 --> 51:59.742
Do you have any idea
who could've done this?

51:59.825 --> 52:00.951
Not at all.

52:01.035 --> 52:02.870
[Sol] Did you have a bad breakup recently?

52:02.953 --> 52:05.205
Those kind of exes turn into stalkers--

52:05.289 --> 52:08.208
It's fine. This is a personal matter.
Please get back to work.

52:08.292 --> 52:11.128
We don't know what these weirdos
might do if we leave them be.

52:11.211 --> 52:15.341
He's right. A crazy stalker like this
could pop out of nowhere and do something…

52:15.424 --> 52:17.843
Thanks for your concern,
but I'll deal with it myself.

52:22.348 --> 52:24.975
-[Seung-gyu] We're just worried…
-[Sol] Ms. Song…

52:25.893 --> 52:27.227
-[remote beeps]
-[Sol exclaims]

52:27.311 --> 52:29.897
[exclaims] That darned glass.
She's always turning it…

52:29.980 --> 52:32.608
[whimpers] My pretty hands…

52:32.691 --> 52:34.818
What kind of crazy jerk would do this?

52:37.529 --> 52:39.156
Hang on…

52:39.239 --> 52:41.659
[running]

52:42.660 --> 52:43.869
[door opens]

52:43.952 --> 52:46.163
[Hayeong] Haran. I mean, Ms. Song
since we're at work.

52:46.872 --> 52:48.540
The stalker who sent those photos…

52:48.624 --> 52:52.044
Maybe it's the same guy
who called your name in the street.

52:53.504 --> 52:54.755
Right, ma'am?

52:54.838 --> 52:56.799
He could've been following you,

52:56.882 --> 52:59.802
and he could've yelled your name
by accident when you were in danger.

53:03.305 --> 53:07.059
-If you're done, get back to work.
-Work isn't important right now.

53:07.142 --> 53:08.477
[sighs]

53:14.274 --> 53:17.111
All right, Ms. Song.

53:22.866 --> 53:25.828
-What are you doing?
-There's a smudge on it.

53:25.911 --> 53:26.912
Just a second.

53:27.621 --> 53:28.664
I'll excuse myself.

53:31.041 --> 53:32.042
[door opens]

53:32.668 --> 53:33.794
[door closes]

53:34.294 --> 53:36.130
[Haran] If the stalker who sent the photos

53:36.755 --> 53:38.882
is the same guy who called my name…

53:39.967 --> 53:41.176
Seonu Chan?

53:41.260 --> 53:43.262
[♪ pensive music playing]

53:46.056 --> 53:47.099
[soft bark]

53:50.644 --> 53:51.645
WON CHARACTER CONCEPT

53:51.729 --> 53:53.981
[Hayeong] Ms. Kim said that
Won resembles my sister…

53:54.064 --> 53:56.608
I mean, Lead Designer Song Haran.

53:57.609 --> 53:59.903
[Haran] If the character
is based on the type of girl he likes,

54:00.446 --> 54:03.407
maybe he saw that I looked similar
when he came to Korea

54:03.490 --> 54:05.451
and learned my name after stalking me.

54:06.285 --> 54:09.204
Then, he followed me to the art exhibit
and witnessed the accident.

54:11.039 --> 54:13.208
I bet he didn't know
we'd be working together.

54:14.126 --> 54:15.127
[gasps]

54:15.586 --> 54:17.045
Is that why he reacted like that?

54:17.629 --> 54:20.007
Right.

54:20.716 --> 54:21.925
It's…

54:23.177 --> 54:24.428
It's nice to meet you.

54:24.511 --> 54:27.181
[Haran] It's because it wasn't
his first time seeing me.

54:28.098 --> 54:31.268
-[scoffs]
-Emergency ice water for you.

54:31.351 --> 54:35.022
You seemed frustrated
about something. [chuckles]

54:35.105 --> 54:37.608
The ice machine
stopped acting up. [chuckles]

54:38.358 --> 54:42.237
One of my regulars who's really handy
dropped by and fixed it instantly.

54:42.738 --> 54:43.989
Thank you.

54:44.072 --> 54:45.407
[cell phone buzzes]

54:48.368 --> 54:50.204
[Nana] There's an urgent meeting
with a client.

54:50.287 --> 54:54.291
Come to Grand Lumiere Hotel
by 7:00 p.m. tonight.

54:57.127 --> 54:58.879
WON CHARACTER CONCEPT

55:00.214 --> 55:01.340
[scoffs]

55:02.633 --> 55:05.802
"SHIM"
Coffee House

55:05.886 --> 55:07.596
[hums, grunts]

55:09.264 --> 55:10.891
[sighs]

55:13.143 --> 55:14.311
[sighs]

55:15.312 --> 55:17.356
-[customer] Hello.
-Hey!

55:17.439 --> 55:20.442
My VVIP regular who fixed my ice machine.

55:20.526 --> 55:22.402
Come on in. [chuckles]

55:22.486 --> 55:23.862
[in English] Welcome.

55:23.946 --> 55:25.781
[in Korean] Hi, Genius.

55:25.864 --> 55:28.075
Here. Sit down.

55:28.575 --> 55:29.952
I'll make you some coffee.

55:30.035 --> 55:31.662
Okay. Thank you.

55:32.204 --> 55:33.205
Genius, wait.

55:33.664 --> 55:34.665
[whines]

55:37.626 --> 55:40.003
[Manjae] Did you go to the art exhibit?

55:40.087 --> 55:42.464
You said you'd go right away
when I gave you the ticket.

55:43.006 --> 55:44.007
Uh…

55:44.633 --> 55:46.969
Yes. Thank you for the ticket.

55:47.803 --> 55:51.682
But for someone
who always smiles so handsomely,

55:52.307 --> 55:54.518
why do you look so gloomy today?

55:54.601 --> 55:56.436
-[chuckles]
-Uh… [inhales sharply]

55:56.520 --> 55:58.480
[exclaims] Right?

55:58.564 --> 56:01.149
I'm usually really handsome,

56:01.858 --> 56:05.070
but I didn't get much sleep,
so I guess I look less handsome today.

56:05.862 --> 56:07.447
Why didn't you get much sleep?

56:07.531 --> 56:09.908
Did you have a nightmare?

56:09.992 --> 56:11.034
[chuckles]

56:11.660 --> 56:13.287
[breathes deeply]

56:14.705 --> 56:15.789
[Chan] Oh.

56:15.872 --> 56:17.291
Do you play the harmonica?

56:17.374 --> 56:18.584
Oh, that. [chuckles]

56:19.167 --> 56:21.253
I found it while cleaning out my clutter.

56:22.296 --> 56:26.008
I get out of breath easily now,
so my chest hurts.

56:26.091 --> 56:27.634
I can't play it so well anymore.

56:27.718 --> 56:29.219
-Here.
-Thank you.

56:29.303 --> 56:33.015
I used to play that often
in my neighborhood when I was little.

56:33.098 --> 56:34.558
Where's your hometown?

56:34.641 --> 56:36.268
Chuncheon.

56:36.351 --> 56:38.520
All I did was find one old object,

56:38.604 --> 56:41.898
but it reminded me of my old hometown

56:41.982 --> 56:43.275
and my childhood friends.

56:43.358 --> 56:50.365
It came with a full package
of old memories. [chuckles]

56:52.409 --> 56:54.244
Memories…

56:54.828 --> 56:55.871
[clicks tongue]

56:56.747 --> 56:59.625
are kind of like sausage links.

56:59.708 --> 57:01.501
What? Sausage links?

57:02.461 --> 57:03.462
Yes.

57:04.338 --> 57:06.423
Even if you think
you've forgotten everything,

57:06.506 --> 57:08.425
recalling just one memory…

57:10.510 --> 57:12.220
seems to bring everything else along.

57:13.096 --> 57:14.306
Like sausage links.

57:20.395 --> 57:21.396
Hey.

57:22.189 --> 57:23.440
Wait just a moment.

57:25.859 --> 57:26.943
-Okay.
-Hang on.

57:38.330 --> 57:40.457
[creaking]

57:48.048 --> 57:51.677
[♪ playing Baroque music, J.S. Bach
"Goldberg Variations, BWV 988: Aria"]

58:09.236 --> 58:11.279
[♪ Baroque piano music continuing]

58:33.552 --> 58:35.429
[lively chatter]

58:35.512 --> 58:37.139
What kind of meeting is it?

58:37.222 --> 58:38.348
I should at least know…

58:38.432 --> 58:40.934
I told you I'd set you up
on a date with Photographer Yoon.

58:41.017 --> 58:42.018
No.

58:44.730 --> 58:47.232
If that's what this is, I'm not attending.

58:47.983 --> 58:48.984
I'm sorry.

58:50.193 --> 58:52.362
How long do I have to see you
act like this?

58:57.617 --> 58:59.035
It's been seven years.

58:59.119 --> 59:02.497
Everyone gets back up and lives
after going through immense pain.

59:02.998 --> 59:04.374
You're the only one who refuses to.

59:05.250 --> 59:08.462
Are you going to keep running away
from everything like a coward?

59:10.338 --> 59:12.674
You can survive
with at least one person to rely on.

59:12.758 --> 59:14.885
But with no one, you'll crumble.

59:16.511 --> 59:20.432
Mr. Yoon can be someone like that for you.
He's a good man, so--

59:20.515 --> 59:22.517
I don't need a good man!

59:24.186 --> 59:25.896
How can you…

59:26.480 --> 59:28.607
Of all people, how can you do this to me?

59:30.442 --> 59:32.027
I'm the one who wants to live like this.

59:32.569 --> 59:34.488
I feel comfortable this way.

59:36.031 --> 59:39.701
I know, okay?
I know I shouldn't live like this.

59:40.577 --> 59:43.330
I know I'm being stupid and weird.

59:44.164 --> 59:45.415
But…

59:46.792 --> 59:48.084
I'm too scared.

59:48.168 --> 59:50.253
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

59:50.337 --> 59:54.508
I don't want to end up
being anxious and worried every day

59:55.133 --> 59:58.720
that something might happen
to someone I care about.

59:59.846 --> 01:00:01.973
So just let me live like this.

01:00:03.600 --> 01:00:07.187
If there's no one by my side,
at least nothing bad will happen.

01:00:10.148 --> 01:00:11.650
[exhales shakily]

01:00:53.608 --> 01:00:54.985
[tires screeching]

01:00:55.068 --> 01:00:57.028
Dad! Mom!

01:00:57.112 --> 01:00:59.114
Dad! Dad!

01:00:59.865 --> 01:01:01.908
Dad! Mom…

01:01:01.992 --> 01:01:04.870
Mom, get up! Mom!

01:01:04.953 --> 01:01:06.580
Oh, my God!

01:01:06.663 --> 01:01:08.456
Help!

01:01:08.540 --> 01:01:09.666
No, Mom…

01:01:09.749 --> 01:01:12.544
Mom!

01:01:13.837 --> 01:01:15.463
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

01:01:22.137 --> 01:01:23.179
Haran.

01:01:23.263 --> 01:01:25.515
I can't believe what happened. Hmm?

01:01:28.768 --> 01:01:29.936
Grandma.

01:01:31.354 --> 01:01:32.856
Mom, Dad,

01:01:33.940 --> 01:01:35.191
and Chan…

01:01:36.151 --> 01:01:37.611
Even Chan is gone.

01:01:39.863 --> 01:01:42.699
Chan is dead, too. [sobbing]

01:01:49.247 --> 01:01:52.250
Haran, let's go home. Okay?

01:01:53.418 --> 01:01:57.088
Chan is dead too, Grandma.

01:02:00.008 --> 01:02:01.801
Chan…

01:02:02.427 --> 01:02:04.262
Chan is dead, too.

01:02:06.848 --> 01:02:08.516
[crying] Grandma…

01:02:25.909 --> 01:02:26.910
[cell phone buzzes]

01:02:33.959 --> 01:02:36.378
[Nana] At least show Mr. Yoon
some basic courtesy.

01:02:39.130 --> 01:02:40.256
[sighs]

01:02:40.340 --> 01:02:43.718
[♪ Baroque music playing, J.S. Bach
"Goldberg Variations, BWV 988: Aria"]

01:02:43.802 --> 01:02:44.803
[sighs]

01:02:45.971 --> 01:02:49.975
[♪ continues playing Baroque music
on piano]

01:03:15.959 --> 01:03:16.960
[Chan] Oh.

01:03:17.544 --> 01:03:20.296
-I'm sorry. I played without permission.
-[exclaims]

01:03:20.380 --> 01:03:22.215
[in English] Bravo! [chuckles]

01:03:22.799 --> 01:03:25.468
[in Korean] Will you have
some wine with me?

01:03:28.513 --> 01:03:31.141
There's some sediment in this wine,

01:03:31.766 --> 01:03:34.477
so let's drink this
after it settles in a bit.

01:03:34.561 --> 01:03:35.562
Okay.

01:03:36.146 --> 01:03:39.024
By the way, I guess you like Bach.

01:03:39.107 --> 01:03:40.442
No.

01:03:40.525 --> 01:03:42.902
I just happened to hear about the song.

01:03:42.986 --> 01:03:46.906
Someone told me it's good for insomnia.

01:03:46.990 --> 01:03:48.908
Seeing your expression,

01:03:48.992 --> 01:03:50.994
I'm guessing today's the kind of day

01:03:51.745 --> 01:03:54.372
when your memories come flooding back.

01:03:55.999 --> 01:03:58.168
From the way they're coming back to me,

01:03:59.919 --> 01:04:01.921
I guess I haven't forgotten about them.

01:04:02.005 --> 01:04:04.591
-[♪ soft emotional music playing]
-They were just…

01:04:05.508 --> 01:04:07.010
buried for a while.

01:04:08.428 --> 01:04:09.804
[Manjae] Mmm.

01:04:10.513 --> 01:04:14.184
The thing about memories
is that sometimes…

01:04:17.312 --> 01:04:19.022
they're really rebellious.

01:04:19.105 --> 01:04:22.984
The more you try to forget,
the more vivid they become.

01:04:23.068 --> 01:04:27.822
And when you want to remember,
they run away from you.

01:04:29.824 --> 01:04:31.743
So don't strain yourself.

01:04:31.826 --> 01:04:34.704
Just try leaving them be.

01:04:35.330 --> 01:04:39.459
Just like this wine,
memories get cloudy if you disturb them.

01:04:39.959 --> 01:04:45.173
But if you leave them be,
they'll eventually become clearer.

01:04:46.299 --> 01:04:47.300
[Manjae chuckles]

01:04:48.426 --> 01:04:50.428
[♪ soft music continuing]

01:04:50.512 --> 01:04:51.554
[chuckles]

01:04:52.013 --> 01:04:53.014
All right.

01:04:53.848 --> 01:04:57.185
I'll try to just leave them be.

01:04:57.268 --> 01:04:58.394
-Let's drink.
-Okay.

01:04:59.312 --> 01:05:00.522
[glass clinks]

01:05:04.526 --> 01:05:05.985
I'm sorry.

01:05:06.069 --> 01:05:10.198
I'll talk to Ms. Kim and make sure
this mistake doesn't happen again.

01:05:10.281 --> 01:05:14.244
I came to say that you don't have
to waste your time on me.

01:05:15.662 --> 01:05:16.663
[Yoon] Yes, I know.

01:05:17.622 --> 01:05:21.000
I know you don't have any feelings for me,
but I really am sincere…

01:05:21.084 --> 01:05:22.168
Are you kidding me?

01:05:22.252 --> 01:05:25.255
Right. I understand
you don't want to hear it.

01:05:25.338 --> 01:05:27.006
But I really am sincere--

01:05:27.090 --> 01:05:29.509
I'm sincerely sorry,
but something urgent came up.

01:05:29.592 --> 01:05:31.469
-I'll get going. I'm sorry.
-Excuse me?

01:05:31.553 --> 01:05:34.347
[stutters] Ms. Song!

01:05:51.364 --> 01:05:52.365
What?

01:05:52.991 --> 01:05:54.200
Why are you…

01:05:54.284 --> 01:05:56.369
Could you say my name?

01:05:57.078 --> 01:06:00.081
-What?
-You're the one who called my name

01:06:00.165 --> 01:06:02.750
in front of the art museum
on the 16th, right?

01:06:04.335 --> 01:06:06.504
I met you for the first time
a few days ago.

01:06:07.422 --> 01:06:09.090
How long have you known me?

01:06:12.886 --> 01:06:15.680
Tell me how you know me.

01:06:16.681 --> 01:06:18.266
What are you hiding?

01:06:22.979 --> 01:06:24.772
[Chan] Someone I have to meet…

01:06:24.856 --> 01:06:27.275
[♪ soft emotional song playing]

01:06:28.359 --> 01:06:31.237
Someone who brought me back to life

01:06:33.031 --> 01:06:34.032
and seems to hold…

01:06:35.283 --> 01:06:38.161
the keys to my life.

01:06:39.996 --> 01:06:41.956
[♪ soft emotional song continuing]

01:06:47.837 --> 01:06:51.299
The seasons of life
don't always come in order.

01:06:52.217 --> 01:06:54.802
Sometimes, the moment
you feel like it's spring,

01:06:57.388 --> 01:07:00.433
a harsh winter suddenly arrives.

01:07:04.229 --> 01:07:05.313
Seven years ago,

01:07:07.357 --> 01:07:08.900
in the midst of my coldest winter,

01:07:09.651 --> 01:07:12.111
she came into my life
like a warm spring breeze.

01:07:12.904 --> 01:07:14.489
And now, she's here again.

01:07:15.823 --> 01:07:18.493
And that day, we had no idea

01:07:19.160 --> 01:07:22.580
whether our future seasons
would be warm like spring

01:07:23.331 --> 01:07:26.000
or harsh like winter.

01:07:33.007 --> 01:07:34.592
Seonu Chan…

01:07:37.053 --> 01:07:38.096
who are you?

01:07:40.348 --> 01:07:41.516
[Haran] I love you, Chan.

01:07:43.268 --> 01:07:44.435
I love you,

01:07:45.770 --> 01:07:46.980
Kang Hyeokchan.

01:07:49.857 --> 01:07:51.859
[♪ soft emotional song continues]

01:07:53.695 --> 01:07:56.114
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:08:18.052 --> 01:08:19.053
[song ends]

01:08:20.221 --> 01:08:23.349
[Haran] Mr. Seonu.
Why are you stalking me?

01:08:23.433 --> 01:08:25.226
[Chan] It feels like
it's hard to get close to her.

01:08:25.768 --> 01:08:28.146
[Manjae] She never talks about herself.

01:08:28.229 --> 01:08:30.064
[Haran] How did you know
I don't like eggplants?

01:08:30.148 --> 01:08:33.067
There's another guy who speaks like him.

01:08:33.151 --> 01:08:34.527
[Chan] Why does this keep happening?

01:08:34.610 --> 01:08:35.820
It's scaring me.

01:08:36.195 --> 01:08:38.239
[Haran] What are you doing here?

01:08:38.323 --> 01:08:39.699
[Chan] I'm going to live here.

01:08:39.782 --> 01:08:42.327
[Nana] They look good together.

01:08:42.410 --> 01:08:45.330
Keep an eye on Ms. Song

01:08:45.413 --> 01:08:47.290
and Seonu Chan.

01:08:51.544 --> 01:08:53.546
[♪ theme music playing]

01:08:59.427 --> 01:09:00.428
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:09:00.511 --> 01:09:01.512
Translated by Juyoung Park
